# Applies whenever a Docker build's context is the repo root (e.g. Nixpacks/
# buildpack builds for backend and admin-panel that don't scope down to their
# own subfolder). Keeps build-context transfer small regardless of how each
# service's Build Path/Docker Context Path is configured in Dokploy.
#
# Deliberately excludes only whole directories/files no service needs, never
# broad extension patterns — safer against accidentally stripping an asset
# a service actually depends on (e.g. landing/assets/*.png).

.git/
.github/
.agents/
.codex/
.vscode/

# Not needed by any deployed service's build
mobile/
docs/
qr-samples/
app logos/
README.md
color-used.md
prompt.md
502343394_17843970039499162_6070394078534669840_n.jpg

# Dependency/build artifacts (already gitignored, excluded here too in case
# a build ever runs against an unclean local checkout)
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
**/build/
**/.dart_tool/
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# OS/editor cruft
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
